    "rawResponseText": "Hotel-branded residences in the Caribbean and Latin America are concentrated in the luxury and upper-upscale segments. The brands most commonly encountered include:\n\n### Most established and recurring\n- **The Ritz-Carlton / Ritz-Carlton Reserve** — Marriott International  \n- **Four Seasons**\n- **St. Regis** — Marriott International  \n- **Rosewood**\n- **Fairmont** — Accor  \n- **W Hotels** — Marriott International  \n\nThese consistently rank among the leading hotel-residence brands across the Americas. Earlier region-specific research likewise identified Four Seasons, Ritz-Carlton, Rosewood and Aman as Caribbean leaders, with Ritz-Carlton, St. Regis, Four Seasons and Rosewood prominent in Latin America’s pipeline. ([pdf.savills.com](https://pdf.savills.com/documents/BR_Americas_GT19.pdf))\n\n### Other prominent luxury brands\n- **Aman**\n- **One&Only**\n- **Mandarin Oriental**\n- **Banyan Tree**\n- **Six Senses** — IHG\n- **Waldorf Astoria** and **Conrad** — Hilton\n- **Raffles** — Accor\n- **Park Hyatt, Andaz and Thompson** — Hyatt\n- **JW Marriott, EDITION and Autograph Collection** — Marriott International\n\nSavills’ broader 2025–2026 data identifies Ritz-Carlton, Four Seasons, St. Regis, Mandarin Oriental, W, Rosewood, Fairmont, Aman and Six Senses among the world’s leading hotel-residential brands. Marriott is the largest parent group in the sector overall. ([pdf.savills.com](https://pdf.savills.com/documents/Savills-Branded-Residences-Annual-Report-2025-2026.pdf))\n\n### Lifestyle and resort-oriented names also encountered\n- **SLS**\n- **Nobu**\n- **Auberge Resorts Collection**\n- **Montage**\n- **Viceroy**\n- **Fasano**, especially in Brazil\n- **Kempinski**\n- **Hard Rock**\n\nIn practical terms, a Caribbean or Latin American developer’s primary luxury-brand comparison set would usually begin with **Four Seasons, Ritz-Carlton, St. Regis, Rosewood, Fairmont and W**, then expand to brands such as **Aman, One&Only, Mandarin Oriental, Waldorf Astoria, Six Senses and Banyan Tree**, depending on the destination, price positioning and resort concept. Luxury hotel brands remain the dominant category, while international operators continue using residences to expand in Mexico, the Caribbean and major Latin American cities. ([pdf.savills.com](https://pdf.savills.com/documents/BR_Americas_GT19.pdf))",
